WEBVTT

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:12.012
"Sorawo and Toriko"

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:31.448
<i>School never taught me what friends are</i>

00:00:31.448 --> 00:00:36.828
<i>People are such difficult creatures</i>

00:00:36.828 --> 00:00:41.250
<i>This world where you never</i>
<i>know what's said behind your back</i>

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:46.797
<i>Looks a little ugly to me</i>

00:00:46.797 --> 00:00:51.677
<i>Compassion and ego sway on the scales</i>

00:00:51.677 --> 00:00:56.223
<i>They've swayed ever since I met you</i>

00:00:56.223 --> 00:00:59.142
<i>Your trespassing did a number on me</i>

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:03.438
<i>It's not like anyone would do</i>

00:01:03.438 --> 00:01:03.522
<i>Is your empathy and complicity just an act?</i>

00:01:03.522 --> 00:01:04.690
"Kisaragi"
"Katasu - Yami"
<i>Is your empathy and complicity just an act?</i>

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:08.944
<i>Is your empathy and complicity just an act?</i>

00:01:08.944 --> 00:01:13.282
<i>Like a fish out of water</i>

00:01:13.282 --> 00:01:15.576
<i>Delicacy and literacy</i>

00:01:15.576 --> 00:01:18.161
<i>Might not be necessary</i>

00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:21.331
<i>I just want to be wanted</i>

00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:23.750
<i>Selfish little me</i>

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:27.921
<i>The scales have tipped</i>

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:30.174
<i>As friends</i>

00:01:30.174 --> 00:01:36.180
<i>Let's meet in a secret place</i>

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.653
Could this be...?

00:01:51.653 --> 00:01:53.322
Sorawo?

00:02:10.506 --> 00:02:13.091
Kakandara.

00:02:13.091 --> 00:02:14.551
That's her!

00:02:14.551 --> 00:02:18.805
She's the one we saw!

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.390
Toriko, shoot her! Quick!

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:22.142
On it!

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.352
Shoot!

00:02:23.352 --> 00:02:25.437
Shoot, shoot!

00:02:39.743 --> 00:02:41.995
Attack! Attack! Keep shooting!

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:44.957
We gotta kill it! Shoot!

00:03:04.518 --> 00:03:07.354
I thought it was her!

00:03:07.354 --> 00:03:07.688
There's an urban legend
about three juvenile delinquents

00:03:07.688 --> 00:03:09.523
"Do Not Enter"
There's an urban legend
about three juvenile delinquents

00:03:09.523 --> 00:03:15.529
"Do Not Enter"
who enter a forbidden forest and
encounter a half-human, half-snake monster.

00:03:15.529 --> 00:03:18.282
"Do Not Enter"
That monster's name is Kankandara.

00:03:18.282 --> 00:03:18.699
That monster's name is Kankandara.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:23.120
Fire! Shoot! Shoot!

00:03:46.185 --> 00:03:49.521
This is bad. If we don't do something...

00:03:54.443 --> 00:03:56.153
Toriko!

00:03:56.153 --> 00:03:59.031
We need something bigger.
See what they've got!

00:03:59.031 --> 00:04:01.658
Got it! I'll be right back!

00:04:01.658 --> 00:04:04.703
Why's that thing staring at me?

00:04:04.703 --> 00:04:07.456
Is it trying to intimidate
me so I look away?

00:04:07.456 --> 00:04:10.834
We can't attack it unless
I can see its true form.

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:13.670
It wants to shut down my right eye!

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:15.839
I'm not scared of some backwoods punk!

00:04:15.839 --> 00:04:17.966
I'm gonna look you right in the eye!

00:04:17.966 --> 00:04:22.679
Not only that, I'll kill you!
I'm gonna murder you with my eye!

00:04:37.778 --> 00:04:42.658
Just a little longer. Toriko's getting
something that will do serious damage.

00:04:42.658 --> 00:04:46.245
One and done! You'll be history!

00:05:06.348 --> 00:05:08.809
Attack! Now!

00:05:19.945 --> 00:05:23.323
Finish it!

00:05:43.385 --> 00:05:44.845
We got it.

00:05:44.845 --> 00:05:45.804
Is it dead?

00:05:45.804 --> 00:05:48.432
Is it dead?

00:05:48.432 --> 00:05:51.852
We... We did it.

00:05:52.853 --> 00:05:55.147
Sorawo! Are you all right?

00:05:55.147 --> 00:05:58.066
I did say we needed
something bigger, but...

00:05:58.066 --> 00:06:01.153
That was the biggest thing they had.

00:06:01.153 --> 00:06:04.072
That's just like you.

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:12.539
Drake, doesn't this place look familiar?

00:06:12.539 --> 00:06:15.584
Yes, it certainly does.

00:06:15.584 --> 00:06:18.420
This is where we crossed
over to the Otherside.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:21.590
I don't know how I forgot.

00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:27.596
They say memory impairment can
result from a horrific experience.

00:06:27.596 --> 00:06:32.935
You guys probably encountered that
monster when you first came here.

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:38.524
Let's go home...

00:06:38.524 --> 00:06:41.860
...before something more horrific happens.

00:06:48.242 --> 00:06:51.203
Would you grab on around there?

00:06:51.203 --> 00:06:52.079
Here?

00:06:52.079 --> 00:06:53.330
Yeah.

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:55.791
Try walking while holding it.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:00.879
What is it?

00:07:00.879 --> 00:07:02.297
It's a gate!

00:07:02.297 --> 00:07:04.132
The gate?

00:07:09.221 --> 00:07:13.559
All right, marines. Let's go home!

00:07:13.559 --> 00:07:15.936
Please, hurry.

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:24.236
Thanks! The girls!

00:07:24.236 --> 00:07:27.531
The girls are lifesavers!

00:07:27.531 --> 00:07:31.535
Hey, the girls!
Get yourself out of here, too.

00:07:33.495 --> 00:07:37.624
That felt like a lifetime
supply of gratitude.

00:07:37.624 --> 00:07:39.418
But...

00:07:39.418 --> 00:07:41.336
What's with "the girls"?

00:07:41.336 --> 00:07:43.964
Sounds like some lame girl band.

00:07:43.964 --> 00:07:47.551
What's wrong with that?
I think it's kind of cool.

00:07:47.551 --> 00:07:51.180
We got this far thanks to you two.

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:52.931
We are truly grateful.

00:07:52.931 --> 00:07:54.808
No worries.

00:07:54.808 --> 00:07:56.351
You better hurry.

00:07:56.351 --> 00:07:58.353
Right. Thanks.

00:07:58.353 --> 00:08:00.522
The girls...

00:08:00.522 --> 00:08:04.151
I hold your courage in high regard.

00:08:06.737 --> 00:08:08.822
Oh, one more thing!

00:08:08.822 --> 00:08:10.324
What is it?

00:08:10.324 --> 00:08:15.204
How many casualties did you
suffer since we left your base camp?

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.290
Zero.

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:21.668
Your rescue operation
was a complete success.

00:08:21.668 --> 00:08:24.171
Really?

00:08:25.589 --> 00:08:28.258
Well, it's just you two now.

00:08:28.258 --> 00:08:31.178
Sorry. This is as far as we go.

00:08:31.178 --> 00:08:32.429
Goodbye.

00:08:32.429 --> 00:08:34.515
See you!

00:08:34.515 --> 00:08:36.850
Hey, what are you--?

00:08:44.525 --> 00:08:46.151
Nice work, Toriko.

00:08:46.151 --> 00:08:48.779
You, too, Sorawo.

00:08:48.779 --> 00:08:49.863
You all right?

00:08:49.863 --> 00:08:52.241
Yeah, sorry.

00:08:52.241 --> 00:08:53.408
I'm exhausted.

00:08:53.408 --> 00:08:54.701
Whoa there.

00:08:54.701 --> 00:09:00.999
That was scary hard, but we got
everyone out of here alive.

00:09:00.999 --> 00:09:02.334
Huh?

00:09:02.334 --> 00:09:07.339
What's going on? Hold on. What is this?

00:09:08.715 --> 00:09:11.718
You were amazing, Sorawo.

00:09:11.718 --> 00:09:17.057
I did it because you said
you wanted to rescue them.

00:09:17.057 --> 00:09:20.519
Keep this up and you'll spoil me.

00:09:20.519 --> 00:09:25.983
Honestly, I didn't really care about them.

00:09:25.983 --> 00:09:29.570
I'd forgotten about them
until you brought it up.

00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:35.367
I mean, I'm only interested in myself.
I don't care about others.

00:09:35.367 --> 00:09:40.205
That's not true.
You've got a really kind heart.

00:09:40.205 --> 00:09:42.082
More than Kozakura?

00:09:42.082 --> 00:09:44.626
That bothered you?

00:09:44.626 --> 00:09:47.671
Sorry for getting upset.

00:09:47.671 --> 00:09:49.798
What're you...?

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:54.428
I love watching you try your hardest.

00:09:54.428 --> 00:09:57.139
Wh-What's happening?

00:09:57.139 --> 00:10:02.769
I feel like things I could never do myself
are possible if I'm with you, Sorawo.

00:10:02.769 --> 00:10:05.063
But...

00:10:05.063 --> 00:10:09.067
I could say the same about you, Toriko.

00:10:09.067 --> 00:10:11.028
Wait a sec.

00:10:11.028 --> 00:10:15.657
Is that why you always
order more than you can eat?

00:10:15.657 --> 00:10:20.204
Because you know if you can't finish,
I'll try my best to help?

00:10:21.413 --> 00:10:25.083
You might be on to something!

00:10:25.083 --> 00:10:27.085
I knew it.

00:10:27.085 --> 00:10:30.005
I almost started to cry.

00:10:30.005 --> 00:10:32.758
What do you mean almost?

00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:36.178
Let's get out of here.

00:10:36.178 --> 00:10:40.390
Yeah, let's go. But how?

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:44.019
If we go back this way,
we'll run into those soldiers again.

00:10:44.019 --> 00:10:45.521
That'd be awkward.

00:10:45.521 --> 00:10:46.647
I know, right?

00:10:46.647 --> 00:10:48.524
Well, let's look around a bit.

00:10:48.524 --> 00:10:50.526
Good call!

00:10:50.526 --> 00:10:53.153
What do wanna eat when we celebrate?

00:10:53.153 --> 00:10:54.530
We just went out yesterday.

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:59.076
So what? Let's celebrate again,
just the two of us.

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:21.974
It's still there.

00:11:21.974 --> 00:11:23.475
We're gonna use it.

00:11:23.475 --> 00:11:26.019
Yeah, we'll take it to the Otherside.

00:11:26.019 --> 00:11:27.187
How?

00:11:27.187 --> 00:11:31.942
We'll find a gate big enough
and take it through there.

00:11:31.942 --> 00:11:34.695
Just get it the hell off my doorstep!

00:11:34.695 --> 00:11:37.614
If it's not gone in three days,

00:11:37.614 --> 00:11:40.367
I'll make you use it to cut
the grass at Shakujii Park.

00:11:40.367 --> 00:11:42.202
Then I'll make you smoke it.

00:11:42.202 --> 00:11:45.205
Huh?

00:11:45.205 --> 00:11:48.125
If you don't like it,
go find a goddamn gate!

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:53.505
"Imamura Coffee"

00:11:53.505 --> 00:11:56.258
It's sure hard finding a gate.

00:11:56.258 --> 00:11:58.468
I thought we'd find one nearby.

00:11:58.468 --> 00:12:01.180
But it's never that easy.

00:12:02.431 --> 00:12:04.099
They serve beer here.

00:12:04.099 --> 00:12:08.645
No, it's still too early. If we
start drinking now, it's all over.

00:12:08.645 --> 00:12:10.814
Then let it be over.

00:12:14.276 --> 00:12:15.277
No, no!

00:12:15.277 --> 00:12:17.613
Regardless of the AP-1,

00:12:17.613 --> 00:12:20.407
wouldn't it be nice to
find an easy-to-use gate?

00:12:20.407 --> 00:12:25.454
Yeah. Who knows how long we
can use the elevator in Jinbo-cho.

00:12:25.454 --> 00:12:30.667
I wonder if there's a gate we can get
through quickly and is easily accessible.

00:12:30.667 --> 00:12:34.296
If only we knew what places
with gates had in common.

00:12:34.296 --> 00:12:36.924
It'd be easier to find them.

00:12:47.601 --> 00:12:51.063
Hey, we'll end up back at
Kozakura's if we head this way.

00:12:51.063 --> 00:12:51.897
Nothing yet?

00:12:51.897 --> 00:12:54.107
Nope.

00:12:54.107 --> 00:12:56.818
Would've been great
to have one around here.

00:12:56.818 --> 00:13:00.322
We wouldn't have to move the AP-1 too far.

00:13:01.365 --> 00:13:03.534
This sucks.

00:13:03.534 --> 00:13:06.662
It'll just sit there forever
if we don't do something.

00:13:06.662 --> 00:13:09.122
Can we buy the land where it's parked?

00:13:09.122 --> 00:13:11.083
No way. The money to buy it--

00:13:11.083 --> 00:13:12.876
It's right there.

00:13:12.876 --> 00:13:14.545
What? The money?

00:13:14.545 --> 00:13:15.379
A gate!

00:13:15.379 --> 00:13:16.463
No way! Where?

00:13:16.463 --> 00:13:18.048
Over there.

00:13:23.387 --> 00:13:24.304
Around here?

00:13:24.304 --> 00:13:25.764
Yeah.

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:36.525
Wow, jackpot! But why here?

00:13:36.525 --> 00:13:38.443
Beats me.

00:13:42.072 --> 00:13:43.156
That's it!

00:13:43.156 --> 00:13:44.491
Hm?

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:52.791
Right. That's when it
first opened up here.

00:13:52.791 --> 00:13:55.919
But if Kozakura finds out...

00:13:55.919 --> 00:13:58.130
Something wrong?

00:14:11.894 --> 00:14:14.938
Yes! It started!

00:14:14.938 --> 00:14:17.316
High five!

00:14:23.488 --> 00:14:25.407
She's still mad.

00:14:25.407 --> 00:14:30.037
Well, there <i>is </i>an Otherside
entrance right on her doorstep, so...

00:14:30.037 --> 00:14:33.290
You gotta be kidding me.
Why me? This can't be happening.

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:36.126
This can't be happening.
This can't be happening.

00:14:36.126 --> 00:14:39.630
I doubt anything will come
through unless I force it open.

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:42.341
What about the old ladies?

00:14:42.341 --> 00:14:45.552
She'll have to cuddle Ponpoko
and weather the storm.

00:14:45.552 --> 00:14:49.389
We don't want to lose a
super-convenient gate like this.

00:14:49.389 --> 00:14:50.933
Yeah.

00:14:52.518 --> 00:14:53.769
Okay, here goes.

00:14:53.769 --> 00:14:55.687
Let's do it!

00:15:08.992 --> 00:15:09.701
--It works!

00:15:09.701 --> 00:15:10.619
--Hurry!
--It works!

00:15:10.619 --> 00:15:13.121
Even I can drive this!

00:15:13.121 --> 00:15:17.167
Can't it go any faster?
That was a super-chill pace.

00:15:17.167 --> 00:15:20.170
Well, it is a piece of farming equipment.

00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:21.755
It'd be faster to walk.

00:15:21.755 --> 00:15:24.883
But we wouldn't have to.

00:15:24.883 --> 00:15:27.553
Isn't this empty space a waste?

00:15:27.553 --> 00:15:31.265
Let's buy some hooks to hold our stuff.

00:15:31.265 --> 00:15:34.184
We can stow stuff up there, too.

00:15:34.184 --> 00:15:36.687
That's a good place for our rifles.

00:15:36.687 --> 00:15:40.816
It's really living up to
its all-purpose moniker.

00:15:40.816 --> 00:15:43.235
I bet it's gonna come in handy.

00:15:43.235 --> 00:15:47.072
No one could've imagined it would
be used in a strange new world,

00:15:47.072 --> 00:15:51.118
least of all, whoever created it.

00:15:51.118 --> 00:15:53.328
Okay, see you later.

00:15:53.328 --> 00:15:57.082
I don't know how you guys
can go off like it's nothing.

00:15:57.082 --> 00:16:00.002
We're just dropping it off.
We'll be right back.

00:16:00.002 --> 00:16:03.213
Sounds like certain death to me.

00:16:03.213 --> 00:16:07.968
Don't bring back anything weird
this time. This is <i>my </i>house after all.

00:16:07.968 --> 00:16:09.261
Yes, ma'am.

00:16:09.261 --> 00:16:10.929
Maybe we <i>should </i>buy the land.

00:16:10.929 --> 00:16:13.557
There's that money issue, remember?

00:16:13.557 --> 00:16:15.309
Toriko, the gate, please.

00:16:15.309 --> 00:16:16.935
Got it.

00:16:25.319 --> 00:16:26.737
Here we go!

00:16:26.737 --> 00:16:29.114
Full speed ahead!

00:16:35.495 --> 00:16:37.831
Morons.

00:16:38.874 --> 00:16:41.293
What's up?

00:16:42.419 --> 00:16:47.674
Huh? Where are Sorawo and Toriko?
I thought I heard their voices.

00:16:47.674 --> 00:16:50.010
Not my problem!

00:17:07.236 --> 00:17:09.238
Stop, stop!

00:17:17.788 --> 00:17:19.706
Hey, look.

00:17:19.706 --> 00:17:22.251
Didn't we first meet around here?

00:17:22.251 --> 00:17:26.296
I have no idea. There are
no landmarks or anything.

00:17:26.296 --> 00:17:28.257
That's true.

00:17:31.176 --> 00:17:34.972
How long have we known each other?

00:17:34.972 --> 00:17:39.643
It was May in our world,
so I guess about three months?

00:17:39.643 --> 00:17:41.728
Just three months.

00:17:41.728 --> 00:17:47.109
It's strange.
It feels like we go way back.

00:17:51.947 --> 00:17:56.535
Really? Yeah... I guess.

00:18:01.081 --> 00:18:03.292
I was wondering.

00:18:03.292 --> 00:18:06.086
Why do you hang out with me?

00:18:06.086 --> 00:18:07.379
Huh?

00:18:07.379 --> 00:18:10.716
You've got zero interest in Satsuki.

00:18:10.716 --> 00:18:16.471
Yet here you are with me
in such a dangerous place.

00:18:16.471 --> 00:18:18.307
Why?

00:18:20.559 --> 00:18:23.270
Why? Well...

00:18:24.688 --> 00:18:27.065
I do like to explore.

00:18:27.065 --> 00:18:30.569
And I was drawn to the
Otherside before I met you.

00:18:30.569 --> 00:18:32.779
Plus...

00:18:35.532 --> 00:18:39.494
You know, y-you're my friend.

00:18:41.205 --> 00:18:42.915
Thanks.

00:18:44.124 --> 00:18:49.213
But are you all right with me
having you all to myself?

00:18:49.213 --> 00:18:51.757
What do you mean?

00:18:51.757 --> 00:18:56.678
You're friends with Kozakura and Akari.

00:18:56.678 --> 00:19:01.642
And you worked so hard to
rescue those American soldiers.

00:19:01.642 --> 00:19:02.976
You should be out there,

00:19:02.976 --> 00:19:06.563
meeting new people and
expanding your horizons.

00:19:06.563 --> 00:19:08.398
But...

00:19:08.398 --> 00:19:13.529
if you're stuck with just me,
I'd feel like I was holding you back.

00:19:14.863 --> 00:19:20.661
No. I don't want to expand my horizons,
and I don't like meeting new people.

00:19:20.661 --> 00:19:22.162
That's such a waste.

00:19:22.162 --> 00:19:24.498
No, it's not.

00:19:24.498 --> 00:19:26.625
Where's this even coming from?

00:19:26.625 --> 00:19:29.711
Well, I guess I was like that, too.

00:19:29.711 --> 00:19:31.421
Huh?

00:19:31.421 --> 00:19:35.467
Satsuki was the only one
who mattered to me.

00:19:35.467 --> 00:19:40.722
I wasn't interested in anyone else.

00:19:40.722 --> 00:19:46.395
I didn't even care if everyone
except Satsuki were to vanish.

00:19:48.981 --> 00:19:52.484
But then it was Satsuki who vanished.

00:19:52.484 --> 00:19:56.822
I was cast all alone
into a world without her.

00:19:56.822 --> 00:20:00.617
The sheer thought was
too terrifying to bear.

00:20:00.617 --> 00:20:03.787
You? Afraid?

00:20:03.787 --> 00:20:05.914
I thought that

00:20:05.914 --> 00:20:08.834
I'd have to live alone forever.

00:20:11.086 --> 00:20:13.463
Alone?

00:20:13.463 --> 00:20:16.508
What happens if I die here?

00:20:17.676 --> 00:20:22.222
That's what I was thinking
right before I met Toriko.

00:20:22.222 --> 00:20:25.809
I wanted to be alone.

00:20:28.312 --> 00:20:33.108
When I discovered the Otherside,
I was excited to have a world all my own.

00:20:33.108 --> 00:20:35.819
I started running around like crazy.

00:20:35.819 --> 00:20:39.698
The next thing I knew, I couldn't move.

00:20:39.698 --> 00:20:45.245
That's when I thought,
"I bet no one would notice I was gone."

00:20:45.245 --> 00:20:50.626
I didn't feel sad or scared
or anything like that.

00:20:53.003 --> 00:20:56.590
But then I met you, Toriko.

00:20:56.590 --> 00:21:00.135
I felt like I was in a
mystical, sparkly embrace.

00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:06.975
I think maybe... I was happy.

00:21:06.975 --> 00:21:09.520
Really? About what?

00:21:10.979 --> 00:21:14.024
N-Nothing! Never mind!

00:21:18.946 --> 00:21:24.576
I still miss Satsuki.
I wish I could see her.

00:21:24.576 --> 00:21:29.498
But I'm not afraid anymore,
though I don't know why.

00:21:37.047 --> 00:21:39.258
You don't say.

00:21:41.426 --> 00:22:02.281
<i>Alone under a sky that softly</i>
<i>fades into the distance</i>

00:22:03.323 --> 00:22:30.475
<i>A dream I had, forgotten in</i>
<i>a memory gap of childhood</i>

00:22:30.475 --> 00:22:40.986
<i>Like a newborn child, a feeling unknown</i>

00:22:40.986 --> 00:22:44.239
<i>Like a newborn child, a feeling unknown</i>
You think it's okay to leave the
AP-1 there while we're gone?

00:22:44.239 --> 00:22:46.491
<i>Like a newborn child, a feeling unknown</i>
It's probably okay.
It'll be out of the rain.

00:22:46.491 --> 00:22:46.783
<i>Like a newborn child, a feeling unknown</i>
<i>     </i>
Right. Well, should we head back?

00:22:46.783 --> 00:22:48.744
<i>Through the town we race</i>
<i>together toward the wind</i>
Right. Well, should we head back?

00:22:48.744 --> 00:22:50.329
<i>Through the town we race</i>
<i>together toward the wind</i>
Yeah.

00:22:50.329 --> 00:22:57.085
<i>Through the town we race</i>
<i>together toward the wind</i>

00:22:57.085 --> 00:22:58.253
<i>Through the town we race</i>
<i>together toward the wind</i>
When's our next visit?

00:22:58.253 --> 00:23:01.048
<i>Through the town we race</i>
<i>together toward the wind</i>
Any time's fine, but we've
got something to do first.

00:23:01.048 --> 00:23:02.549
<i>Through the town we race</i>
<i>together toward the wind</i>
Oh, the party?

00:23:02.549 --> 00:23:03.383
<i>Through the town we race</i>
<i>together toward the wind</i>
The celebration!

00:23:03.383 --> 00:23:06.345
<i>Through the town we race</i>
<i>together toward the wind</i>
Sounds good.
Let's invite Kozakura and Akari.

00:23:06.345 --> 00:23:07.346
<i>Through the town we race</i>
<i>together toward the wind</i>
But we'll split the bill.

00:23:08.263 --> 00:23:11.600
I'm not alone anymore.

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:21.652
<i>Please don't try to find us</i>

00:23:23.987 --> 00:23:26.490
"Prime-Cut Meat Restaurant Bigyu"

00:23:26.865 --> 00:23:29.326
All you can eat? What a great idea!

00:23:29.326 --> 00:23:32.621
Thanks for treating us again!

00:23:32.621 --> 00:23:36.959
You can treat me to the finest meat
for letting you keep the AP-1 at my place.

00:23:36.959 --> 00:23:47.030
Split the bill? Yeah, right!
